/*!

\page position-plugin-corelocation.html
\title Qt Positioning Core Location plugin
\ingroup QtPositioning-plugins

\brief Wraps iOS and macOS positioning subsystems.

\section1 Overview

The Qt Positioning Core Location plugin wraps native Apple Core Location APIs
and provides access to positioning information.

The plugin can be loaded by using the provider name \b corelocation.

\section1 Parameters

The following table lists parameters that \e can be passed to the Core Location
plugin.

\table
\header
    \li Parameter
    \li Description
\row
    \li allowAutoPause
    \li It determines if the plugin allows the system to pause location updates
        automatically to save power when the app is in the background. The default
        value is \c true.
        This parameter is only relevant for iOS when background location updates
        are enabled. See \l {Automatic pausing of location updates} section for
        more details.
\endtable

\section2 Automatic pausing of location updates

In iOS, the underlying \c CLLocationManager can pause location updates
automatically to save battery power when location data is unlikely to change.

If the \c {allowAutoPause} plugin parameter is set to \c {false}, the plugin
sets the \c pausesLocationUpdatesAutomatically property to \c NO on the
\c CLLocationManager instance. This prevents the operating system from pausing
location updates while the application runs in the background.

\note This parameter only affects iOS applications when background location
updates are enabled (by including the \c {location} value in \c UIBackgroundModes
in the \c Info.plist file).

\section1 Examples

The following examples show how to create a \b corelocation \l PositionSource from
C++ and QML.

\section2 QML

The following snippet creates a \l PositionSource with no parameters. The default
value for \c {allowAutoPause} is used (\c true).

\qml
PositionSource {
    name: "corelocation"
}
\endqml

The next snippet explicitly adds the \c {allowAutoPause} \l PluginParameter
and sets its value to \c false.

\qml
PositionSource {
    name: "corelocation"
    PluginParameter {
        name: "allowAutoPause"
        value: false
    }
}
\endqml

\section2 C++

The following snippet shows how to use C++ to create a
\l {QGeoPositionInfoSource}{position source} with \c {allowAutoPause} disabled.

\code
QVariantMap params;
params["allowAutoPause"] = false;
QGeoPositionInfoSource *positionSource = QGeoPositionInfoSource::createSource("corelocation", params, this);
\endcode

*/
